== Live workflow view ==

The table above remains the authored source. Cargo provides a computed operational view over the same records:

{{#cargo_query:
 tables=Knowledge_requests
 |fields=Request,Status,Candidate_domains,Needed_depth,Canonical_page
 |order by=Status,Request
 |format=table
 |limit=200
}}

Use [[Special:CargoTables]] / [[Special:Drilldown]] for deeper operational inspection after the table has been created on the deployed wiki.

== Request lifecycle ==

<pre>
missing signal
→ request
→ source gathering
→ research
→ draft coherent page
→ verify identity + provenance + claims
→ canonicalize
→ satisfy request + link canonical page
→ update portal/category/core-coverage views
</pre>

A request in <code>requested</code>, <code>researching</code>, <code>drafting</code>, or <code>review</code> remains non-canonical. Repository workflow validation rejects an active request whose proposed title already exists as a Main-namespace page. This makes the request/canon boundary executable rather than advisory.

A <code>satisfied</code> request must link to the resulting canonical page. A declined request remains evidence that the gap was considered rather than disappearing from history.

== Sensitive topics ==

A missing current-political or religious page is not automatically a coverage defect. Apply [[BITwiki:Sensitive topic scope research]] before promoting high-conflict/current material into the queue or public navigation.

